From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:44:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: clear all plane pipe configs before splitting a
 plane

dpu_plane_split() fills pstate->pipe_cfg[] for the mixer pairs (stages)
of the new topology only. A duplicated plane state still carries the
rectangles of the previous commit, so when a modeset moves a CRTC from
four layer mixers (two stages) to two or one, the configs of the second
stage are left in place. The resource assignment, the clock calculation
and the SSPP checks walk all PIPES_PER_PLANE entries and skip only those
with an empty source rectangle, so the stale rectangles still reserve
SSPPs and count towards the plane clock.

Clear the whole array before it is rebuilt.

This only matters once STAGES_PER_PLANE is 2 (quad-pipe). With a single
stage the loop rewrites both entries on every call.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
index b088ffa4f96..76fdaec8886 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -884,6 +884,9 @@ static int dpu_plane_split(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	u32 num_lm;
 	int stage_id, num_stages;
 
+	/* Rebuild all derived rectangles: a modeset can use fewer mixer pairs. */
+	memset(pstate->pipe_cfg, 0, sizeof(pstate->pipe_cfg));
+
 	max_linewidth = pdpu->catalog->caps->max_linewidth;
 
 	/* In non-virtual plane case, one mixer pair is always needed. */
